* Project Overview :
This repository contains a fully automated Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) pipeline built via GitHub Actions. The pipeline enforces high code 
reliability by running automated verification checks and dynamically packaging the web application into an isolated Docker container, which is then automatically securely 
shipped directly to DockerHub upon verified code updates.

############# CI ########################
- I wrote application code, json file for installing dependencies. Dockerfile to dockerised image. and workflow main.yml to run pipeline as following steps:
1. pipeline will start when pushed anything in application code. set path and push on 
2. INstalled project dependencies
3. run the container 
4. push image on DockerHub

* Architecture Design & Lifecycle
[ Push to main (index.js) ]
          │
          ▼
┌───────────────────────────────────┐
│     Job 1: Test & Validate        │  ◀── Runs on Hosted Ubuntu VM
├───────────────────────────────────┤
│ 1. Checkout Source Code           │
│ 2. Initialize Node.js v20         │
│ 3. Install App Dependencies       │
│ 4. Run Automated Test Suite (npm) │
└───────────────────────────────────┘

              (Success)
          │
          ▼
┌───────────────────────────────────┐
│     Job 2: Build & Deploy         │  ◀── Only runs if Job 1 succeeds
├───────────────────────────────────┤
│ 1. Setup Docker Buildx Environment│
│ 2. Authenticate with DockerHub    │  ◀── Uses encrypted GitHub Secrets
│ 3. Compile Production Container   │  ◀── Optimizes via alpine footprint
│ 4. Push tagged image to Cloud     │  ◀── Tags: 'latest' & Commit SHA
└───────────────────────────────────┘

